    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can provide a brief overview of labor profiles for each region you mentioned. \n\nIn Vietnam and Southeast Asia, you can expect a highly disciplined and hardworking workforce with a strong emphasis on teamwork and reliability. However, wages are relatively low, which may require some adjustments in product pricing. Polish and Romanian workers are also known for their reliability, but wages can be competitive with Western European standards. In contrast, West and Central African countries like Nigeria and Kenya have a more informal labor market, and wages can be lower, but also come with higher risks of labor disputes and management challenges.\n\nManagement styles and oversight requirements tend to be similar globally, but cultural differences can affect how tasks are prioritized and communication takes place. A well-integrated management system and support staff can mitigate some cultural obstacles and ensure effective oversight.",
