      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so basically you're saying the volatility there is more about the people and the local way of doing things vs the more \"structured\" approach in SE Asia or Europe. if we were to go with the African options, would we need to essentially hire a much heavier layer of local supervisors just to keep things on track and make sure people are actually showing up and following protocols? it feels like there's a fundamental difference in the \"caliber\" of the workforce compared to the other regions.",
